    "deathDate": "1844-03-01",
    "bio": "a Representative from Massachusetts; born in Roxbury, Mass., July 5, 1763; graduated from Harvard University in 1784; engaged in agricultural pursuits; member of the Massachusetts state house of representatives 1794-1802; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Eighth and to the four succeeding Congresses (March 4, 1803-March 3, 1813); unsuccessful candidate for reelection in 1812 to the Thirteenth Congress; member of the Massachusetts state constitutional convention in 1820; again a member of the Massachusetts state house of representatives in 1822, 1823, and 1826; died in Roxbury, Mass., March 1, 1844; interment at Forest Hills Cemetery, Boston, Mass.",
